  "notes": "Sheet 0 (FL Interiors, a high-floor vacation apartment in the Armani/Casa residential tower, Sunny Isles Beach, Florida; all six photographs are interiors): a tone-on-tone minimalist apartment with the serenity of a spa - floor-to-ceiling glass wall and a curving corner onto the Atlantic and neighbouring towers, glossy cream porcelain floors, a round recessed ceiling coffer over the living room, a curved wall of vertical oak slats with a veined marble feature wall and fireplace, a long curved kitchen island under glossy white cabinets, two curved white bouclé sofas round a round table on a pale rug, an oval dining table with blush upholstered chairs under a brass linear chandelier, and a reeded grey-blue wall in the dining room. Modelled as a cutaway set (like Living N5) on a floor plate over the sea: floor, glass walls with mullions and balcony rail, a ceiling beam round the edge only (the ceiling is left off so the room can be seen into), the slatted wall, marble wall, kitchen island, sofas, rug, dining table and chairs. The tower itself is not shown in the photographs and is not modelled; the apartment's floor and plan are guessed (a 20 x 12 m plate). A private apartment in a residential tower, placed at its town only (Sunny Isles Beach)."
